@startuml websocket_connection_scope_comparison
title WebSocket Connection Scope Comparison

' OpenClaw baseline: b015925bc30f6a8363f290b07d5f8588e21422b8, Gateway Protocol v4
' Source: docs/gateway/protocol.md (Gateway protocol, exact session subscriptions)
' Source: packages/gateway-protocol/src/schema/logs-chat.ts (ChatSendParamsSchema, ChatEventSchema)
' Source: src/gateway/server-broadcast.ts (createGatewayBroadcaster)
' pi-mono-java baseline: 1f7a5423219edfa4519d8719f1cc8a188ed72873
' Source: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/mode/server/ServerMode.java (configureRoutes)
' Source: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/mode/server/ChatWebSocketHandler.java (handle)
' Source: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/mode/server/SessionPool.java (getOrCreate)
' Target source: pi-mono-java-manager-driven-multi-agent-runtime/README.md (WebSocket v2 target)
' Target source: pi-mono-java-manager-driven-multi-agent-runtime/chat-ws-v2.asyncapi.yaml
' Observed behavior: OpenClaw uses one Gateway connection for requests and events across sessions.
' Current Java behavior: one connection captures one AgentSession selected by a query parameter.
' Target design: one CampusAgent connection is bound to one caller-owned session and agent after connect.
' Target design: globally unique session_id is the only Runtime session key; tenant and user stay upstream.
' Target design: one Pod permits one active read/write connection per session; resume replaces the old generation.
' Target design: RuntimeSessionStore persists authority in a database; active runs remain Pod-local.
' Design reason: Session scope fixes authorization, model, disclosure, and audit boundaries.

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
left to right direction

package "OpenClaw - implemented" as openclaw {
  actor "Gateway client" as oc_client
  component "Gateway connection" as oc_conn
  component "Gateway control plane" as oc_gateway
  database "Session A" as oc_session_a
  database "Session B" as oc_session_b
  component "Node and control APIs" as oc_control

  oc_client --> oc_conn
  oc_conn --> oc_gateway : Request/Response/Event Frames
  oc_gateway --> oc_session_a : sessionKey=A
  oc_gateway --> oc_session_b : sessionKey=B
  oc_gateway --> oc_control : methods and events
}

package "pi-mono-java v1 - current" as java_v1 {
  actor "Chat client" as java_client
  component "WebSocket connection" as java_conn
  component "ChatWebSocketHandler" as java_handler
  database "AgentSession" as java_session
  database "SessionPool\nkey: conversation_id" as java_pool

  java_client --> java_conn : query conversation_id
  java_conn --> java_handler
  java_handler --> java_pool
  java_pool --> java_session
}

package "CampusAgent v2 - target only" as campus_v2 {
  actor "mate-service or server SDK" as cc_client
  component "Trusted gateway\nuser-IP affinity" as cc_edge
  component "Current connection\ngeneration N" as cc_conn
  component "Replaced connection\ngeneration N-1" as cc_old_conn
  component "ManagedSessionPool" as cc_pool
  component "ManagedRunHub" as cc_hub
  database "Session 1 / immutable Agent A" as cc_session
  database "RuntimeSessionStore\ndatabase authority" as cc_store

  cc_client --> cc_edge : wss service call
  cc_edge --> cc_conn : full path, same Pod
  cc_conn --> cc_pool : globally unique session_id
  cc_pool --> cc_old_conn : close 4409 SESSION_REPLACED
  cc_pool --> cc_session
  cc_session --> cc_hub : zero or one active run
  cc_pool --> cc_store : persist session and history
}

note bottom of openclaw
  One connection may address many sessions.
  Exact subscription, scope, and visibility filters apply.
end note

note bottom of java_v1
  Session identity is not agent-qualified.
  new_session changes the captured session.
end note

note bottom of campus_v2
  session_id is supplied and managed upstream.
  Tenant and user identities stay upstream.
  Agent binding is immutable after create.
  One Pod has one active read/write connection.
  There is no observer connection or Redis owner.
  IP changes and Pod restart break active-run continuity.
end note
@enduml

@startuml websocket_handshake_comparison
title WebSocket Handshake and Authentication Comparison

' OpenClaw baseline: b015925bc30f6a8363f290b07d5f8588e21422b8, Gateway Protocol v4
' Source: docs/gateway/protocol.md (Handshake, authentication, protocol versioning)
' Source: docs/gateway/clients.md (scopes, pairing, capabilities)
' Source: packages/gateway-protocol/src/schema/frames.ts (ConnectParamsSchema, HelloOkSchema)
' pi-mono-java baseline: 1f7a5423219edfa4519d8719f1cc8a188ed72873
' Source: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/mode/server/ServerMode.java (configureRoutes)
' Source: docs/asyncapi/chat-ws.yaml (query parameters and v1 messages)
' Target source: pi-mono-java-manager-driven-multi-agent-runtime/chat-ws-v2.asyncapi.yaml
' Observed behavior: OpenClaw emits a challenge before the first client connect Request Frame.
' Current Java behavior: the route reads conversation_id and creates or resumes a session immediately.
' Target design: CampusAgent authenticates the Upgrade and then requires connect within five seconds.
' Target design: the trusted internal gateway validates existing private-key/JWT service authentication.
' Target design: private keys never travel; inbound credentials are not forwarded to Managers.
' Target design: /agent-service/v1/ws/chat is the full gateway and service path.
' Target design: URL v1 is the service API version; connect protocol 2 is the Frame version.
' Target design: a wss URI starts establishment; the WebSocket exists only after HTTP 101.
' Target design: HTTP 101 and the connect RequestFrame are different handshake layers.
' Target design: typed structured delta is intrinsic to protocol v2; only full_thinking is optional.
' Design reason: service credentials stay in transport authentication and never enter chat payloads.

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
autonumber

actor "OpenClaw client" as OC
participant "OpenClaw Gateway" as OG
actor "Java v1 client" as JV1C
participant "ServerMode" as SM
participant "ChatWebSocketHandler" as CWH
actor "mate-service or server SDK" as CC
participant "Trusted internal gateway" as EDGE
participant "agent-service Chat endpoint" as V2
participant "Agent and Model Managers" as MGR

== OpenClaw implemented ==
OC -> OG : WebSocket Upgrade
OG --> OC : event connect.challenge {nonce, ts}
OC -> OG : req connect {minProtocol, maxProtocol,\nauth, device, role, scopes, caps}
OG --> OC : res payload hello-ok {protocol, features,\npolicy, snapshot}
note over OC,OG
The challenge is a server event.
The first client frame is connect.
Device identity and pairing support broad Gateway access.
end note

== pi-mono-java v1 current ==
JV1C -> SM : Upgrade /api/ws/chat?conversation_id=...
SM -> CWH : handle(exchange, conversationId)
CWH --> JV1C : WebSocket accepted; no protocol hello
note over JV1C,CWH
The v1 AsyncAPI documents a token query parameter.
The baseline route shown here extracts only conversation_id.
There is no connect protocol negotiation.
end note

== CampusAgent v2 target: HTTP opening handshake ==
CC -> CC : call WebSocket library\nconnect(wss URI)
CC -> EDGE : open one TCP connection\nthen TLS\nthen HTTP/1.1 GET\n/agent-service/v1/ws/chat\nexisting signed-JWT integration
EDGE -> EDGE : validate service JWT and Upgrade\nprivate key never travels
EDGE -> V2 : preserve full path, principal, and Upgrade
V2 --> EDGE : accept WebSocket Upgrade
EDGE --> CC : HTTP/1.1 101 Switching Protocols

== CampusAgent v2 target: application handshake ==
CC -> V2 : WebSocket Text Frame within 5 seconds\nreq connect {mode, session_id, agent_id,\nmodel_id?, traceparent?}
V2 -> MGR : target-audience access token\nauthorize agent and resolve model
MGR --> V2 : effective identity and model
V2 --> CC : res payload {protocol=2, connection_id,\ngeneration, session, limits, features, active_run?}
note over CC,V2
No business query parameter and no URL token.
Browsers cannot call this endpoint directly.
End-user identity stays in mate-service.
The wss URI requests establishment; it is not an open WebSocket.
The HTTPS form is a handshake target, not a REST API.
HTTP 101 creates transport; connect binds the session.
The connection cannot switch agent or session.
URL v1 and Frame protocol 2 are independent versions.
Inbound JWT is never forwarded to a Manager.
Unknown capabilities are ignored and not echoed.
Typed structured delta is not a capability.
full_thinking is optional and policy-gated.
Effective features do not replace request authorization.
end note
@enduml

@startuml websocket_stream_recovery_comparison
title Stream and Recovery Comparison

' OpenClaw baseline: b015925bc30f6a8363f290b07d5f8588e21422b8, Gateway Protocol v4
' Source: src/gateway/server-chat.ts (resolveBroadcastDelta, emitChatDelta)
' Source: src/gateway/server-broadcast.ts (createGatewayBroadcaster, per-client seq, slow consumers)
' Source: docs/gateway/protocol.md (sessions.messages.subscribe)
' Source: docs/gateway/clients.md (re-subscribe, chat.history, inFlightRun)
' pi-mono-java baseline: 1f7a5423219edfa4519d8719f1cc8a188ed72873
' Source: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/mode/server/ChatWebSocketHandler.java (mapEventToJson, close handling)
' Target source: pi-mono-java-manager-driven-multi-agent-runtime/README.md (ManagedRunHub)
' Target source: pi-mono-java-manager-driven-multi-agent-runtime/chat-ws-v2.asyncapi.yaml
' Observed behavior: OpenClaw clients recover from sequence gaps by reconnecting and reloading authoritative state.
' Current Java behavior: message_update sends the accumulated message and disconnect aborts streaming.
' Target design: Pool and Hub retain active-run state only inside one Pod; RuntimeSessionStore is database authority.
' Target design: same-Pod resume replaces the connection generation and captures an atomic snapshot.
' Target design: Pod restart rebuilds the session and records interrupted history; it does not continue the active run.
' Design reason: network disconnect must not abort a local run, but v1 does not claim cross-Pod continuation.

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
autonumber

actor "OpenClaw client" as OC
participant "Gateway broadcaster" as OGB
participant "Chat history" as OCH
actor "Java v1 client" as JVC
participant "ChatWebSocketHandler" as JWH
participant "AgentSession" as JAS
actor "mate-service" as CCC
participant "Trusted gateway" as CCG
participant "agent-service Pod A" as CCW
participant "ManagedRunHub" as MRH
database "RuntimeSessionStore" as CCH
participant "agent-service Pod B" as CCB

== OpenClaw implemented ==
OC -> OGB : sessions.messages.subscribe(sessionKey)
OGB --> OC : chat event {seq, runId, sessionKey,\ndeltaText, message?, replace?}
OGB --> OC : later event with sequence gap
OC -> OC : detect connection or run sequence gap
OC -> OCH : chat.history(sessionKey)
OCH --> OC : authoritative messages and in-flight state
note over OC,OGB
Chat delta is a standard event, not capability-gated.
Some chat deltas may be marked dropIfSlow.
A gap is observable because sequence numbers advance.
end note

== pi-mono-java v1 current ==
JAS --> JWH : MessageUpdateEvent(fullMessage, fineGrainedEvent)
JWH --> JVC : message_update {message: fullMessage}
JVC -x JWH : connection closes
JWH -> JAS : abort()
note over JVC,JAS
The wire format does not expose the fine-grained event.
There is no active-run snapshot protocol.
end note

== CampusAgent v2 target only ==
MRH --> CCW : message.updated {run_seq, typed delta}
CCW --> CCC : current delta only
CCC -x CCW : connection closes
note over MRH
The run continues inside Pod A without a subscriber.
end note

alt Same-Pod resume by user-IP affinity
  CCC -> CCG : reconnect and req connect mode=resume
  CCG -> CCW : route full path to Pod A
  CCW -> MRH : increment generation, replace old subscription,\nand atomically capture cursor
  MRH --> CCW : active_run snapshot at run_seq=N\nand history_seq=H
  CCW --> CCC : connect response with generation, frozen config,\npartial message or null, open contents, and tools
  CCC -> CCW : chat.history(runId, through H)
  CCW -> CCH : read database history through H
  CCH --> CCW : prior messages and tool results
  CCW --> CCC : authoritative history
  MRH --> CCW : deltas after N
  CCW --> CCC : ordered message.updated events
else Pod restart or routing to another Pod
  CCC -> CCG : reconnect after Pod A is unavailable
  CCG -> CCB : route to available Pod B
  CCB -> CCH : rebuild Session and Agent
  CCH --> CCB : persisted complete content blocks\nand active RunRecord
  CCB -> CCH : persist Message.status=interrupted\nand RunRecord.outcome=interrupted
  CCB --> CCC : connect response with active_run=null
  CCC -> CCB : chat.history
  CCB -> CCH : read authoritative history
  CCH --> CCB : interrupted Message and RunRecord
  CCB --> CCC : interrupted history
end
note over CCG,CCB
No Redis, Session Header, cross-Pod forwarding,\nor distributed run owner exists in v1.
Unclosed tail content is not guaranteed after restart.
end note
@enduml

@startuml websocket_transport_dependency_inversion_comparison
title WebSocket Transport Dependency Inversion Comparison

' OpenClaw baseline: b015925bc30f6a8363f290b07d5f8588e21422b8, Gateway Protocol v4
' Source: packages/sdk/src/types.ts (OpenClawTransport)
' Source: packages/sdk/src/transport.ts (GatewayClientTransport)
' Source: packages/sdk/src/client.ts (transport injection and delegation)
' Source: src/gateway/server-methods/shared-types.ts (RespondFn, GatewayRequestHandlers)
' Source: src/gateway/server/ws-types.ts (GatewayWsClient)
' Source: src/gateway/server-broadcast.ts (createGatewayBroadcaster)
' pi-mono-java baseline: 1f7a5423219edfa4519d8719f1cc8a188ed72873
' Source: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/mode/server/ChatWebSocketHandler.java (handle)
' Target source: pi-mono-java-manager-driven-multi-agent-runtime/README.md (SessionTransport)
' Observed behavior: OpenClaw SDK clients depend on OpenClawTransport, while server broadcast still operates on WebSocket clients.
' Current Java behavior: ChatWebSocketHandler directly owns session subscription and aborts the run on disconnect.
' Target design: ChatWebSocketAdapter depends on SessionTransport and ManagedSessionTransport owns generation and session semantics.
' Target design: RuntimeSessionStore is the database authority; Pool and Hub remain Pod-local.
' Design reason: protocol adapters must not own session or active-run lifetime.

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
left to right direction

package "OpenClaw client - implemented" as oc_client_pkg {
  component "OpenClawClient" as oc_sdk
  interface "OpenClawTransport\nrequest / events / close" as oc_transport
  component "GatewayClientTransport" as oc_ws_transport
  component "GatewayClient WebSocket" as oc_ws_client

  oc_sdk --> oc_transport
  oc_ws_transport ..|> oc_transport
  oc_ws_transport --> oc_ws_client
}

package "OpenClaw server - implemented" as oc_server_pkg {
  component "Gateway method handlers" as oc_handlers
  interface "RespondFn" as oc_respond
  component "Gateway broadcaster" as oc_broadcast
  component "GatewayWsClient\nwith WebSocket" as oc_server_ws

  oc_handlers --> oc_respond
  oc_broadcast --> oc_server_ws : bufferedAmount / send / close
}

package "pi-mono-java v1 - current" as java_v1_pkg {
  component "ChatWebSocketHandler" as java_handler
  component "AgentSession" as java_agent

  java_handler --> java_agent : subscribe / prompt / abort
}

package "CampusAgent v2 server - target only" as cc_target_pkg {
  component "ChatWebSocketAdapter" as cc_adapter
  interface "SessionTransport\nconnect / request / events / close" as cc_transport
  component "ManagedSessionTransport" as cc_managed
  component "ManagedSessionPool" as cc_pool
  component "ManagedRunHub" as cc_hub
  database "RuntimeSessionStore" as cc_store
  component "Future HTTP and SSE adapter" as cc_sse

  cc_adapter --> cc_transport
  cc_sse --> cc_transport
  cc_managed ..|> cc_transport
  cc_managed --> cc_pool
  cc_managed --> cc_hub
  cc_managed --> cc_store
}

note bottom of oc_client_pkg
  Client-side transport inversion is complete.
end note

note bottom of oc_server_pkg
  Handler response is abstracted.
  Broadcast and client state remain WebSocket-aware.
end note

note bottom of cc_target_pkg
  Adapter maps closed Frames and network backpressure.
  Managed transport owns generation, snapshot, and subscription.
  One Pod has one active read/write connection per session.
  Database history survives restart; active runs do not.
end note
@enduml

@startuml attachment_data_plane_comparison
title Attachment Data Plane Comparison

' OpenClaw baseline: b015925bc30f6a8363f290b07d5f8588e21422b8, Gateway Protocol v4
' Source: packages/gateway-protocol/src/schema/logs-chat.ts ChatAttachmentSchema
' Source: ui/src/pages/chat/attachment-api.ts and chat-send-request.ts
' Source: src/gateway/server-methods/attachment-normalize.ts and chat-send-attachments.ts
' Observed behavior: OpenClaw sends base64 attachment envelopes inside chat.send and validates actual bytes before acknowledgement.
' pi-mono-java baseline: 1f7a5423219edfa4519d8719f1cc8a188ed72873
' Source: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/mode/server/ChatWebSocketHandler.java
' Current Java behavior: the v1 WebSocket prompt accepts text only; general attachment transport is not implemented.
' Target source: campusmate-attachment-service/README.md
' Target source: pi-mono-java-manager-driven-multi-agent-runtime/README.md attachment section
' Target design: CampusMate stores metadata in shared openGauss and immutable bodies in private OBS.
' Target design: agent-service uses internal batch resolve and content streaming, without local files or direct OBS access.
' Design reason: keep the file data plane outside Chat Frames while allowing any service Pod to read authoritative content.

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
left to right direction

package "OpenClaw - implemented" as OpenClawAttachment {
  actor "OpenClaw UI" as OcUi
  component "chat.send Request Frame\nbase64 attachment envelope" as OcFrame
  component "Gateway attachment validation\nand preparation" as OcGateway
  component "Inline or staged model input" as OcInput

  OcUi --> OcFrame : content, MIME, file name, size
  OcFrame --> OcGateway : one WebSocket request
  OcGateway --> OcGateway : decode, sniff, limit, validate
  OcGateway --> OcInput : accepted attachment input
}

package "pi-mono-java v1 - current" as JavaAttachment {
  actor "Java v1 client" as JavaClient
  component "prompt string" as JavaPrompt
  component "ChatWebSocketHandler" as JavaHandler

  JavaClient --> JavaPrompt
  JavaPrompt --> JavaHandler
}

package "CampusAgent v2 - target only" as CampusAttachment {
  actor "Final client" as CampusClient
  component "CampusMate public upload\nand status API" as PublicUpload
  component "CampusMate Attachment Service\nany Pod" as AttachmentService
  database "Shared openGauss\nmetadata and object mapping" as AttachmentDb
  cloud "Private OBS\nimmutable object body" as AttachmentObs
  component "agent-service Pod A" as AgentPodA
  component "agent-service Pod B" as AgentPodB
  database "RuntimeSessionStore\nprojected metadata snapshot" as RuntimeStore

  CampusClient --> PublicUpload : multipart upload and poll READY
  PublicUpload --> AttachmentService
  AttachmentService --> AttachmentDb : metadata transaction
  AttachmentService --> AttachmentObs : write immutable body
  AgentPodA --> AttachmentService : internal batch resolve
  AgentPodB --> AttachmentService : same ID after Pod change
  AgentPodA --> AttachmentService : internal content stream
  AgentPodB --> AttachmentService : internal content stream
  AttachmentService --> AttachmentDb : authorize session and locate object
  AttachmentService --> AttachmentObs : stream body
  AgentPodA --> RuntimeStore : id, name, MIME, size, sha256
  AgentPodB --> RuntimeStore : restore metadata snapshot
}

note bottom of OpenClawAttachment
  The Gateway owns the attachment bytes for this request.
  This is an implemented product boundary, not a defect.
end note

note bottom of JavaAttachment
  General attachment input remains outside the v1 wire contract.
end note

note bottom of CampusAttachment
  WebSocket carries attachment IDs only.
  Resolve returns no object key, URL, or credential.
  Runtime never accesses OBS directly and writes no local file.
  No content_version, reservation, or complex retention claim exists.
end note
@enduml
